# The scene cases of fixtures/src/*.vexp that no toy EXPECT lists, one per line: CASE_ID, a TAB and the reason (plan 04-07; D-172, D-173, amendment A5). scripts/video-check reads this file; a line with no reason is VIDEO_EXEMPT_FORMAT, and the count of lines is printed in the VIDEO_CHECK status line.
# A scene case that a toy EXPECT lists with no second column needs no line here. F0 limit (review fix M-06 of the gate review): F0 perturbs the first number of the first row of a group, so it proves only that the comparison is live; on a frame_flags literal it makes a value no 1-bit flag can hold.
# A group whose only kill is F0 has no other shown kill unless a toy whose evidence shows that group fail is named: the border groups of vce_pal, vce_dot and bg_basic are (vid-palette-mask); the flag groups of video_unmodelled_mode and video_bg_enab are not.
video_vce_pal_golden	golden change detector beside the literal case video_vce_pal, which vid-palette-mask kills (its evidence shows the border group fail)
vid_frame_lines	the divider toy does not change line counts or the frame length: the scene is killed by the faults F4 and F9 of its sweep
video_bg_basic_golden	golden change detector beside the literal cases video_bg_basic_solid and video_bg_basic_asym, which vid-palette-mask and vid-bit-order kill
video_unmodelled_mode	a flag case: the toys leave the line records of the unmodelled frames alone; the flag group declares only F0, which shows the comparison live and no more (recorded limit, review fix M-06); the pix group is killed by F0, F1 and F7 of its fault sweep
video_bg_scroll_asym	killed by F0, F1, F7 and F8 of its fault sweep; the toy vid-scroll-latch moves only the BYR latch rows of video_bg_scroll, and the wrap and direction rows are ASSUMED readings that no mutant of the renderer is spent on (toy cap of 10)
video_bg_enab	killed by F0, F1, F7 and F3 of its fault sweep (the tile rows, the burst frame and the backdrop frame) and by F0 and F8 of the post-toggle rows; the flags group has only F0, a recorded limit (review fix M-06); no toy of the renderer is spent on it (toy cap of 10)
video_spr_basic_solid	killed by the F0, F1 and F7 of its fault sweep (the rows of the sprite index, priority and order groups); the toy cap of 10 of D-173 is reached, so no mutant of the sprite renderer is spent on it
